  "interpretation": "Passing establishes only static agreement on the 128-case, 8-by-16, source-grounded direct-accumulation protocol: K=4 uses a predeclared four-way exact visible-input fork plus one arm-invariant, opening-only, non-binding agenda. The lawyer still receives the complete visible dialogue and compact state, and every attribution-healthy case becomes one complete group-evidence card. Two disjoint map calls extract source-bound modes and one reduce call applies bounded exact edits to a single global playbook. Hard trust gates bind every edit to immutable source artifacts; tied groups can only support failure modes. The next unseen block compares the new playbook version with its exact parent before any teacher call. F/Q, practical safety, exposure, and uncertainty are prequential learning diagnostics and teacher direction; a single block never rolls back the working library or excludes that block from teacher evidence. B8 additionally freezes comparison arms before its increment diagnostic; performance nonpass is reported, while only intervention-isolation failure blocks the accumulated-library freeze. The training-run CN30 entry is only a two-arm Ours-versus-empty mechanism diagnostic. The paper main table instead requires one four-arm controller, one method-independent fixed route artifact, and an immutable external-ready Ours training-source binding made before any CN30 adapter, route, or model call (byte-hash verification remains separately disclosed). Historical method-level CN30 aggregates have already been observed for protocol diagnosis, so a later locked CN30 run is benchmark-aware rather than a pristine confirmatory test; CN30 cases and outcomes remain excluded from the training lawyer and Luna teacher. Bounded same-model action repair is limited to structural, identity, privacy, and leakage failures. Executable low-quality questions reach the client and retain their real question cost, response, reward, warnings, and teacher evidence; they are neither hidden repairs nor distinct termination endpoints. Only lawyer-authored final/abstain actions or the hidden emergency horizon end a session. Reaching that shared safety ceiling is a real, scoreable policy failure that remains in teacher evidence; it is neither healthy success nor an execution-integrity defect. Passing is not evidence of runtime qualification, learned improvement, or benchmark performance."
